title The door that paid its way in
prompt Baton lap as petrichor -- the docs-geode lane and the prose product; the previous lap's recommend named skate/README.md as the next door by reach.
think Round open read clean at 00acc8aa0f. The cold endurance run refused to launch: a stale roster pass from the previous lap held construction/standing-equipment-run.lock.d at pid 2486476, its verdict already fixed at tree_moved because its launch_head was no longer HEAD. The refusal named its own repair.
think I resolved that pid through tools/f/fleet_call.sh rather than pkill -- it read pid 2486476 cwd=/home/keeper/grain-petrichor verdict=dry against six peer trees refused_foreign by working directory. Then --signal TERM, one sent, six refused. The relaunch took the lock.
think The claim board read clear: four peer claims live, none overlapping a prose repair, and this lap opened no new instrument, so nothing to claim.
think prose_register_scan confirmed the previous lap's reading -- skate/README.md at 27 percent, 30 of 109 sentences, the largest repairable body among the fourteen unrostered doors over ceiling, with 563 living citers.
think Reading the 30 with --explain showed eighteen standing inside the owned-bounds list and the proof census: refusal contracts and controls reporting what they plant. That is Meter content sitting inside a page that declares the Door setting.
think The cheap repair was a redeclaration to Field, where 27 percent passes with no edit. The scan's own header had already ruled against that shape: when docs/ joined the roster the room paid its way in rather than buying a raise, and WITNESS_PATTERNS.md went 52 to 29 by restating the incidental negatives while keeping the refusal-subject ones.
think So I restated fourteen incidental sentences and kept sixteen. No sentence was deleted -- the reading holds 109 sentences before and after, which is the check that a ceiling was met by rewriting rather than by cutting.
think Each restatement was checked against the code it describes. The peak bound became at or under, which is the peak <= SkateCoreBounds.lotusSamplePeak guard at skate/Sources/SkateCore/FrameGrid.swift:79 spelled in the tree's own ceiling words rather than in a negation.
think My first rewrap pass was too wide a tool: it reflowed every paragraph over 100 columns, including one I never touched, and split a markdown link across a newline. I reverted and put the wrap inside each replacement string instead, so the diff reaches only the sentences I restated.
think The card read truth_mode=counted, meaning the judged half went unread. I read it: every named error case, every public typealias peer pair, and all six backticked module paths stand in the sources.
obs The page declared the Door setting already, so rostering it cost one path in the DOOR list rather than a page edit. door_documents 22 to 23, front_doors_unrostered_over 14 to 13, door_over_ceiling still 0.
obs The wall was proven from both sides on metal: reverting skate/README.md to its committed bytes made the scan refuse register_drift at exit 1 naming the page and its percentage; restoring the swept page returned verdict=ok at exit 0. A refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass.
obs What stayed is the page's own subject. refuses empty, non-ASCII, over-wide is an initializer's contract; neither hashes content nor claims those bytes came from Grain's crypto is the entire reason the type wears the word Claim. A ceiling met by deleting those would be a worse page at a better number -- the same finding the previous lap wrote about press/README.md's three survivors.
obs No red booked. A low grade is never a red, and nothing on this page was wrong; it was a Door declaration the body had outgrown in one direction.
rota lap 5002, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees. The threshold asks what must stop and what must be cut, and warns that the lap which squints cuts twice. It read directly onto the lock: the refusal named a stale pass, and the choice was to look at what held it rather than route around with a second launch. It read onto the page too -- the redeclaration to Field was the squint, and reading the thirty negatives one at a time was the look.
